      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T15:59:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hey Mark, the situation I\u0027m thinking of is where code gets built on say a 5.10 kernel, but we forget to apply your kernel patch to 6.x where it attempts to run. The ioctl will always exist since the ashmem support comes from android-mainline, but it looks like if we don\u0027t have your ASHMEM_GET_FILE_ID patch then the ashmem_ioctl would return ENOTTY, not EINVAL.",
      "parentUuid": "fc2c87f2_ee791cf0",
      "revId": "bfada115c8f2252e494402b713169cb66b9d7c54",
